CHAPTER III

OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

Article 6

Obligations and responsibilities in the implementation of protection for women and children are the shared responsibility of:
a. regional government;
b. community;
c. family;
d. parents; ande. non-governmental institutions including Customary Institutions and Business Entities.

Article 2

The implementation of PPA is carried out based on the principles of:
a. humanity;

8 -
b. justice and gender equality;
c. protection;
d. best interests of women and children; and
e. non-discrimination.

REGENT OF PULANG PISAU,

Considering:
a. that protection of women and children is an integral part of human rights that must be guaranteed, protected, and respected by the state;
b. that violence against women and children in the Region tends to increase, therefore the Regional Government and/or community need to play an active role optimally to provide protection, so that women and children are prevented and free from violence or threats of violence, torture, or treatment that degrades human dignity and honor;
c. that protection of women and children is a mandatory concurrent affair that is the authority, obligation, and responsibility of the Regional Government, therefore regulation is needed as a basis for the implementation of comprehensive and integrated protection of women and children;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection of Women and Children;

